      {
        "text": "Beth McElroy Kirkwood was appointed to the MWRD Board in December 2024 by Governor JB Pritzker. She has served as Orland Township committeeperson and worked in Orland Park village departments. She also chairs the Moraine Valley Community College Board of Trustees, overseeing a $161 million budget. She supports preserving green space and aligning land-use decisions with environmental stewardship. She also wants to expand the Space to Grow program to suburban townships and schools. As a commissioner, she joined the groundbreaking for the 34th Street Rehabilitation Project in Berwyn.",
